- Implement ETW PID filter descriptor (EVENT_FILTER_TYPE_PID) - requires investigating if goetw/rawsec expose ENABLE_TRACE_PARAMETERS. Would reduce CPU overhead on busy machines by filtering events at kernel level instead of userspace.
- Flag-based CLI (--target, --report, --log, --new-only) to replace positional args. Currently still uses positional args.
- Verify ETW event capture with admin privileges - run probe.exe with admin and check monitor.log for PID field names, event data types, and whether connections appear.
- Consider adding connection duration tracking (time between CONNECT and DISCONNECT events for same endpoint).
- Consider adding DNS resolution correlation - match UDP port 53 traffic with subsequent TCP connections.
- Verify that context cancellation correctly shuts down ETW engines (goetw, rawsec) without resource leaks, now that context is passed from the main application.
- Consider extracting the IP Helper API polling logic from monitor/process.go into a dedicated polling engine component that implements the etw.Engine interface.
- Integration tests exist (goetw, rawsec, iphelper) but require probe.exe built first (`task build`) and ETW tests require admin. Run integration tests manually: `task build && go test ./internal/etw/goetw/ ./internal/etw/rawsec/ ./internal/iphelper/ -v -run Integration` (as admin for ETW tests).
- Add engine-level integration test that starts probe.exe and verifies the full pipeline: engine -> monitors -> report.json with data from all three tools.
- Add doc.go to internal/engine package with comprehensive documentation.